Feature: EN 1993 check outcome of committed documents
  A committed before- or after-snapshot of the mutation fixtures is evaluated by the production report and by an independent clause-table formulation of `../../🔮️oracles/🚦️check-outcome/🐍️.py` (member resistance, flexural and lateral-torsional buckling, class 4 effective sections, the member interaction 6.3.3 Annex B and the 6.2.9 interaction, deflection and joints of the steel members).
  Each row names one check id (a family id reports the worst row of every combination), its status (pass at a utilisation of at most 1, fail above 1) and its utilisation; rows were picked away from the near-limit band so the status is unambiguous.

